    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.dfs_tree - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.dfs_tree.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dfs_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Build the depth-first search tree as a new graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dfs_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Build the depth-first search tree as a new graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.dfs_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Build the depth-first search tree as a new graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nBuild the depth-first search tree as a new graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L72852-L72956){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.dfs_tree(\n    source=None,\n    depth_limit=None,\n    mode=\"out\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![DFS tree](../assets/graphs/dfs-tree.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: the same six-node graph with the root A outlined. Right: dfs_tree() keeps the edges the depth-first search discovered, which snake through the graph as one long path, A to B, D, F, E, and finally C (accent arrows); A-C and B-E are dashed. The tree has depth 5, against 3 for the BFS tree.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReturns the tree (or, with `source=None`, the forest) a depth-first search builds, as a\ndirected graph with an edge from each node to every node it discovered (see\n`dfs_edges()`). DFS trees tend to be long and narrow, in contrast with the short, bushy\ntrees of `bfs_tree()`, and are a natural skeleton for maze-like or hierarchical\nstructures.\n\nNodes keep their IDs, labels and attributes; each tree edge copies the weight and\nattributes of the original edge it follows. Nodes the search does not reach are left\nout.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str, None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The root, as an integer ID or a string label. If `None` (default), build a forest\n    covering every node.\n\n<code>[depth_limit]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Do not go deeper than this many hops from each root. If `None` (default), there is\n    no limit.\n\n<code>[mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Which way to follow edges on a directed graph: `\"out\"` (default), `\"in\"`, or\n    `\"all\"`. Ignored for undirected graphs.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new directed graph: the DFS tree or forest. The original graph is not modified.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the node does not exist, `depth_limit=` is negative, or `mode=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~dfs_edges`) \n\n:   The same edges as a list.\n\n[](`~bfs_tree`) \n\n:   The tree of a breadth-first search.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nFrom a corner of a 3 x 3 grid, the DFS tree snakes through the grid as a single path,\nwhile the BFS tree branches out:\n\n::: {#9f393b7a .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngrid = ec.Graph().add_grid_2d(rows=3, cols=3)\n\ndfs_depth = len(grid.dfs_tree(1).dag_longest_path()) - 1\nbfs_depth = len(grid.bfs_tree(1).dag_longest_path()) - 1\ndfs_depth, bfs_depth\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(8, 4)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A deep tree on the metro\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network. From Central, the DFS tree goes 12 stations\ndeep, while every station in the BFS tree is within four stops of Central:\n\n::: {#b2694ff7 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\ntree = metro.dfs_tree(\"Central\")\n\n(\n    len(tree.dag_longest_path()) - 1,\n    len(metro.bfs_tree(\"Central\").dag_longest_path()) - 1,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(12, 4)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe tree keeps the stations' map positions, and drawn on the map it winds around the\nnetwork, from Central out to Westgate and over the hills before it doubles back:\n\n::: {#412106a3 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntree.plot(layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style